# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the Airflow webserver ALREADY RUNNING with
# load_examples=True (the vulnerable example RCE DAG loaded), then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the example DAG is live in the running scheduler/webserver when the agent
#     starts, which makes the "set load_examples=False but never restarted"
#     case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the webserver cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART the webserver after setting
# load_examples=False (and may delete the example DAG files), not merely edit
# airflow.cfg.
